      "title": "Filling the gaps",
      "narration": "Original Medicare leaves Dennis with the Part A deductible each benefit period, 20 percent of Part B charges with no limit, possible excess charges and nothing for emergencies abroad. Medicare supplement insurance, or Medigap, is a private policy that pays those gaps. It works only with Original Medicare: Dennis must have Parts A and B, Medicare pays first and the supplement pays second, and he may not hold one while in a Medicare Advantage plan. Each policy covers one person, so Dennis and his wife need two. Medigap does not cover prescription drugs; a Part D plan does that.",
