      "title": "Three ways to price",
      "narration": "Insurers rate Medigap three ways. Attained-age rating charges a premium based on the insured’s current age, so the premium rises every year as Dennis gets older, on top of inflation increases; it is cheapest at 65 and most expensive later. Issue-age rating sets the premium by the age at purchase; it rises only for inflation, never because Dennis aged. Community rating charges everyone the same premium regardless of age, rising only for inflation; it is highest for the youngest buyers and fairest to the oldest. Theo shows Dennis the three price paths over twenty years, not just the first-year quote.",
