      "title": "Additional benefits and high-deductible plans",
      "narration": "The richer letters add benefits: the skilled nursing facility coinsurance for days 21 through 100, the Part A deductible, Part B excess charges, and emergency care during foreign travel at 80 percent up to a lifetime limit. Plans C and F also pay the Part B deductible, but federal law closed them to anyone who became eligible for Medicare on or after January 1, 2020, which made Plan G the most comprehensive plan for new enrollees. Plans K and L pay a percentage of some benefits in exchange for an out-of-pocket limit. High-deductible versions of Plans F and G pay nothing until the insured meets an annual deductible, indexed yearly, in exchange for a much lower premium.",
